# Excludes from the Docker build context shipped to the daemon.
# Anything matched here is NOT visible inside the build, regardless of
# whether the Dockerfile would have COPY'd it. Trimming the context
# keeps the per-build upload small and stops a stray .env from
# accidentally landing in an image layer.
#
# Build context: `projects/apex/` (NOT the repo root). The Dockerfile
# re-installs and re-builds inside the image, so every install artifact
# below is rebuilt and must be excluded so a stale host `.next` /
# `node_modules` never shadows the in-image build.
#
# P1-3 RESOLUTION CONTEXT: the Windows host's `.next/standalone` is
# emitted with EPERM symlink warnings (no admin / Developer Mode). By
# excluding `**/.next` here, the host's broken standalone trace can never
# leak into the image — the Linux build stage produces a clean standalone
# from scratch (where symlink tracing works). See DECISIONS.md ADR-005.

# Workspace install + build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
**/playwright/.cache

# Local environment files — secrets. apex needs NO runtime secrets
# (web-only, in-memory mock — ADR-001 / ADR-003); the only config is the
# build-time `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` ARG, set in the Dockerfile, not from
# a checked-in env file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs.
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Test + review surfaces — never executed at runtime.
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/e2e
**/playwright.config.ts
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.lighthouseci
lighthouserc.json
lighthouserc.mobile.json
web/lighthouserc.json
web/lighthouserc.mobile.json

# The RAW source GLB is NOT in the repo and NOT under public/ — it lives
# only on the owner's machine (`Downloads/source/...`, ~31 MB, branded
# Maybach — P0-1). The OPTIMIZED 1.9 MB `web/public/models/apex-suv.glb`
# IS required at runtime (the live R3F configurator + the Tier-3 stills
# are rendered from it) and is intentionally NOT excluded here so it
# ships in the image. When the P0-1 unbadged-GLB swap lands, the same
# `public/models/apex-suv.glb` path is replaced — no .dockerignore change.
# Defensive: never let a raw multi-MB source GLB into the context if one
# is ever dropped under the project tree.
**/source/*.glb
**/*-raw.glb

# Fleet body GLBs (model-swap PASS B) are RENDER-ONLY inputs — the offline
# `render-from-scene.mjs` harness loads them over HTTP from a local
# `next start` to bake the static fleet card AVIFs (`public/renders/<slug>/`).
# The four non-flagship fleet cards are STATIC images at runtime (they are not
# configurable, no live canvas), so these GLBs are never requested by the
# browser in production — exclude them from the image to keep it lean.
web/public/models/fleet

# Dev-time asset/render/screenshot scripts (sharp render pipeline,
# gltf-transform optimizer, capture + verify scripts). Their OUTPUTS are
# committed under `web/public/{models,renders,gallery,maps,og}` and ship;
# the scripts that produced them do not run at runtime.
web/scripts

# Per-project docs — readable on GitHub, not needed in the runtime image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/PLAN.md
**/PROGRESS.md
**/DECISIONS.md
**/AGENT_NOTES.md
**/CREDITS.md
**/TASKS.md
**/CRITIQUE-*.md
**/REVIEW-*.md
**/DEPLOY.md
docs

# The build / deploy descriptors themselves — they tell the build what
# to do; they do not belong inside the resulting image.
fly.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Git metadata — not needed at runtime, and a stray fragment of the
# repo's history in a layer is a leak surface.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
